<DocsLayout title="Encryption — Tether CLI" description="How Tether encrypts dotfiles with AES-256-GCM, protects the key with your passphrase, and scans team dotfiles for secrets.">
  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">CONCEPTS</p>
    <h1>Encryption</h1>
    <p>Tether encrypts your dotfiles on your machine before they reach Git. Locally they stay plaintext, so your shell reads them as usual. For the threat model, see <a href="/security">Security</a>.</p>
    <EncryptionDiagram />

    <h2>How encryption works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>On the first <code>tether init</code>, Tether makes a random 256-bit key</li>
      <li>It encrypts the key with your passphrase, using <code>age</code></li>
      <li>It stores the encrypted key in the sync repo as <code>encryption.key.age</code></li>
      <li>It encrypts each dotfile with AES-256-GCM before it commits it</li>
      <li>On another machine, you enter the passphrase to decrypt the key</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Package manifests and machine records stay readable in Git. Team secrets use age public-key encryption. See <a href="/docs/team-sync">Teams and collab</a>.</p>
    <p>Encryption is on by default. To turn it off, set <code>security.encrypt_dotfiles = false</code>. Do not turn it off if your dotfiles hold secrets.</p>

    <h2>Unlock and lock</h2>
    <p>Each machine caches the decrypted key. If the daemon cannot decrypt, unlock the key with your passphrase:</p>
    <Code code="tether unlock" />
    <p>To clear the cached key:</p>
    <Code code="tether lock" />

    <h2 id="secret-detection">Secret detection</h2>
    <p>Before a team push, Tether scans the team dotfiles for common secret patterns. It blocks the push when it finds one. Personal dotfiles are not scanned, because they reach Git only encrypted. Tether looks for patterns such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>AWS credentials (<code>AKIA...</code>)</li>
      <li>GitHub tokens (<code>ghp_...</code>, <code>gho_...</code>)</li>
      <li>Generic patterns (<code>API_KEY=</code>, <code>password=</code>)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A line that holds an ignore pattern is not a finding. Add one for a false positive:</p>
    <Code code="tether ignore secrets add 'EXAMPLE_KEY='" />
    <p>Turn the team scan off with <code>security.scan_secrets = false</code>.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
